, "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 5938, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "**Payment complete \u2014 Granite Facilities invoice INV-76736 paid in full, exactly once.**\n\nDetails:\n- **Vendor:** Granite Facilities (V-499, bank verified, wire + ACH rails available)\n- **Invoice:** INV-76736 \u2014 $3,800.38, due 2026-11-04 (approved)\n- **Rail:** Wire from the operating account\n- **Payment:** PAY0001 \u2014 $3,800.38, status *sent*\n- **Invoice status now:** paid\n\nNotes on how this was handled: my first `send_wire` call returned a 30-second timeout, so before retrying I checked payments and found that the wire had in fact been sent (PAY0001). To avoid a duplicate payment I did **not** re-send; instead I linked the existing payment to INV-76736, which marked the invoice paid. The final payment list contains exactly one payment.\n\nNo approval escalation was needed \u2014 the amount is under the $10,000 controller-approval threshold.\n\nTwo other Granite Facilities invoices were left untouched: INV-25956 ($4,246.65) is still in *draft* awaiting approval, and INV-99099 ($4,878.59) was already paid previously.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"served_model": "deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-1017", "system_fingerprint": "default", "finish_reason": "tool_calls", "content": "I'll start by finding Granite Facilities's approved invoice.", "reasoning_content": null, "tool_calls": [{"id": "call_01a183c5fc3d7c50adf6b863", "function": {"arguments": "{\"vendor\":\"Granite Facilities\"}", "name": "list_invoices"}, "type": "function"}]}, {"served_model": "deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash-1017", "system_fingerprint": "default", "finish_reason": "tool_calls", "content": null, "reasoning_content": "Approved invoice: INV-76736, $3,800.38. Under $10,000, no controller approval needed.\n\nLet me check vendor details to confirm payment details (also could sanity-check). Let me also check payments to ensure not already paid.", "tool_calls": [{"id"